{
  "rules": [
    "Model exhibits a strong upward bias when recent history is volatile but sentiment remains low (near zero); forecasts consistently overshoot true outcomes by 5-10%.",
    "When sentiment shows alternating positive/negative spikes, the model fails to capture mean reversion and instead projects a linear trend that ignores volatility clustering.",
    "Forecasts systematically underestimate the magnitude of subsequent price spikes; when true outcomes rise sharply (e.g., >90), models remain flat or drift slowly upward.",
    "In low-sentiment regimes with high historical variance, apply a downward correction factor to the forecasted trajectory to account for overconfidence in trend continuity.",
    "Model horizon errors are non-linear: early days show slight underestimation of volatility, but mid-to-late periods show severe overestimation of directional stability."
  ]
}
